+
+Action responses distinguish `queued`/`dispatched` (HTTP 202) from `completed`
+and `error`. A modal `QDialog.exec()` can acknowledge dispatch while the action
+is still running. `completed` means `QAction.trigger()` returned, not that any
+background application work finished. Missing/disabled actions retain their
+errors; invocation exceptions are HTTP 500. An `invocation_id` correlates late
+errors in `get_logs`. Inspect the app and logs before repeating a queued or
+dispatched action; mutating requests are never automatically retried.
